==English==
{{was wotd|2020|September|25}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Edward S. Curtis, Kwakwaka'wakw potlatch, British Columbia.jpg|thumb|A potlatch ''(sense 1)'' of the [[Kwakwaka'wakw|Kwakwakaʼwakw]] [[person|people]] of the [[Pacific Northwest]], photographed by {{w|Edward S. Curtis}} and published in the early 20th century.]]

The {{glossary|noun}} is borrowed from {{bor|en|chn|potlatch}}, {{m|chn|pátlač|t=to give; gift; gift-giving ceremony, potlatch}}, from {{w|Nootka Jargon}} ''pa'chatle'', ''pa'chēētle'', ''pah-chilt'' (“to give, give me”), from {{der|en|nuk|p̕ačiƛ|t=to give a gift during a potlatch ceremony}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=148873|date=December 2006|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref>

Sense 1 of the {{glossary|verb}} (“to give; especially, to give a a gift during a potlatch ceremony”) is borrowed from {{bor|en|chn|potlatch}}, {{m|chn|pátlač}} (see above); sense 2 (“to carry out or take part in a potlatch ceremony”) is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=148874|date=December 2006|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref>

